WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.670
Joe Biden has made another cabinet selection.

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:07.340
It's a very important one because it is the
secretary of Health and Human Services who

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.180
will be coming in during a global hundred
year pandemic.

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.840
And it turns out that Joe Biden has selected
someone who has long supported Medicare for

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:15.840
all.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:16.840
This is very interesting.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:17.840
It's a big deal.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:23.900
And it is Xavier Becerra, who has been chosen
to lead Joe Biden's Department of Health and

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:30.609
Human Services now back in 2017, when when
he was also California attorney general, as

00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:37.050
he still is, Becerra said he would, quote,
absolutely support a Medicare for all plan.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:41.720
Becerra will be leaving his post as California
attorney general.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:44.740
He will be a huge part of fighting the coronavirus
pandemic.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:50.600
He will be a very welcome replacement to the
clownish Trump secretary of HHS, Alex Azar,

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.820
who is just a wild Trump brownnoser.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:59.360
Now, from the standpoint of identity, there
is another first, Xavier Becerra would be

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.880
the first Latino to run HHS.

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:06.210
We're expecting more more health related announcements
from Joe Biden very, very soon.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:09.280
We found out about some of them I mentioned
already.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.869
Secretary of HHS will be Xavier Becerra at
the CDC.

00:01:13.869 --> 00:01:19.289
It will be Rochelle Walensky, the Mass General
Hospital chief of infectious disease here

00:01:19.289 --> 00:01:20.789
in Boston.

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:26.350
Surgeon general will be Dr. Vivek Murthy,
who was also Barack Obama's surgeon general.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:29.440
So these are solid choices, qualified people.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:36.229
Now, I admit what does not make sense to me
about choosing Xavier Becerra for secretary

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:41.100
of HHS is that he does lack experience in
the area of health and medicine.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.590
He's a lawyer now.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:43.889
There's a counterpoint to that.

00:01:43.889 --> 00:01:47.030
Now, it's great that Xavier Becerra has supported
Medicare for all.

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:50.289
I see a lot of Bernie people who like the
choice for that reason.

00:01:50.289 --> 00:01:54.399
But he does lack experience in the field of
medicine.

00:01:54.399 --> 00:02:00.439
On the other hand, he has been front and center
as a lawyer fighting for Obamacare.

00:02:00.439 --> 00:02:05.569
And as I imagine we will see as soon as Joe
Biden is sworn in, Republicans go right back

00:02:05.569 --> 00:02:10.140
to let's get rid of Obamacare, let's get rid
of Obamacare, even though we have no replacement

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:13.040
in that sense, Becerra is a good choice.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:17.920
But remember that Biden doesn't support Medicare
for all anyway.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:21.860
But he does want to expand the Affordable
Care Act to include a public option.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:27.580
And Becerra has experience defending the ACA
in legal settings.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:34.190
And the the other important aspect of this
is that the truth is that secretary of HHS,

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:36.500
you're not really making medical decisions.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:42.900
You're really an executive managing the apparatus
of health and Human Services.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:46.340
And in that sense, there's no way to argue
that Becerra is unqualified.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:51.430
Now, hilariously, there are some Republicans
who have immediately said Becerra is a radical.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:52.430
He's a he's a radical.

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.180
We can't we can't have him running HHS.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:03:00.430
And, of course, you know, those those guidelines
for what counts as radical at this point have

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:03.320
been completely khatuna fired by the right.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:08.460
This also, by the way, take Xavier Becerra
off the list to be the replacement for Kamala

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.010
Harris, whose Senate seat will.

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:15.710
Be vacated when she becomes vice president,
and that's another story which we'll be covering.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:21.680
And lastly, there is a good chance that Basara
will have a tough confirmation fight in the

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:22.680
Senate.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:27.180
I think he will be confirmed because ultimately
he's completely qualified, but I think it

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.570
has the potential to get quite ugly.

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:31.400
Let me know what you think about the selection.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:43.840
I'm on Twitter at 

00:03:43.840 --> 00:04:09.090
David Pakman.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:47.400
I'd love 
to hear from you.

